{"availability":"available","full":"zacwilliamson/gemz","name":"gemz","description":"Explore this public GitHub project.","category":"Other","language":"Ruby","stars":8,"forks":4,"created":"2022-10-07T18:19:59Z","updated":"2023-09-03T15:30:33Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://gemz.onrender.com","topics":[],"demo":"https://gemz.onrender.com/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T20:11:46.454Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T20:11:46.454Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T20:11:46.454Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T00:29:20.265Z","stars":8,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-10T05:41:56.456Z","stars":8,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-15T18:04:18.010Z","stars":8,"forks":4},{"at":"2026-10-19T20:11:46.454Z","stars":8,"forks":4}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A social media experience built with Ruby on Rails. Live Preview","Gemz was created based on The Odin Project's criteria for building a Facebook Clone. My goal was to hit the project specs first, then experiment by adding new features. Writing simple integration and unit tests became an important part of my workflow. This would verify what was or was not working when developing.","Areas I get to improve would be organizing my code, testing, and styling the app properly. My attitude throughout this was to just get it working and then identify blindspots after. If you the reader see areas I can improve, feel free to make an issue or email me at zacwilliamson@icloud.com. I'm always looking to improve my skills."],"features":["utilized Devise so users can register or create new sessions","OAuth allows users to login with Facebook or Github","when a new user signs up, a profile is created with a default color theme","users can add location, link, bio, full name, and profile image (default gravitar image)","users can write posts and attach an image"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zacwilliamson/gemz/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"bece0791b52c639c50518d37416998e93e6fbe